# Industrial bot assets

Read `docs/art/STYLIZED_INDUSTRIAL_ASSETS.md` before bot modeling, material,
baking or export work. Use the linked accepted native renders and references.

- Establish a cohesive structural shell and moving clearances before final bakes.
- Seat mounts, fasteners and addons on actual supporting surfaces.
- Separate broad corner rounds from thin metal chamfers; use real apertures and hardware.
- Bake portable PBR maps with physical edge wear, local assembly AO and explicit repaint coverage.
- Vary shared moving-part wear; preserve connector phases and runtime frames.
- Keep quick previews isolated; require clean import logs, native material/assembly views,
  sampled motion checks and exact artifact hashes before handoff.
- Preserve the user's footprint/contract choices and the A/B ownership split.
- Technical checks do not substitute for requested user visual approval.
